You need to press and release.  If you hold it pressed the booting
will stall, I don't know why.  If you don't get the timing right,
unplug the disk it normally boots from.  Then you'll be dropped at a
prompt.  Give the command "set auto_action halt".  Next time you boot,
it will stop at the SRM prompt.  To boot the system, type "boot".  To
read about some options to boot, do "man boot".

